{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/658905-a-gift-proposal","id":658905,"title":"A Gift proposal.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T21:51:59-07:00","id":658905,"title":"A Gift proposal.","content":"The dragon living in Pangea is a manifestation of the previous Wyrm. Now, Rage is a manifestation of the Wyrm, much like Will belongs to the Weaver and Gnosis is of the Wyld. It seems that a good Level 5 Gift would be one taught by Pangea's that allowed you to substitute Rage for Gnosis. In the Abyss, where using Gnosis powered Gifts is an exercise in futility, this gift would be extremely useful, which makes sense, due to it being a Wyrm Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T22:30:45-07:00","id":658931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/658905-a-gift-proposal#post658905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dragon living in Pangea is a manifestation of the previous Wyrm. Now, <b>Rage is a manifestation of the Wyrm, much like Will belongs to the Weaver and Gnosis is of the Wyld.</b> It seems that a good Level 5 Gift would be one taught by Pangea's that allowed you to substitute Rage for Gnosis. In the Abyss, where using Gnosis powered Gifts is an exercise in futility, this gift would be extremely useful, which makes sense, due to it being a Wyrm Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would take the premise in bold with an entire mine's worth of salt. This correspondence is ultimately arbitrary and often contradicted in books that claim that Rage, for example, is of Luna, or of the Wyld, or etc. There are a lot of ideas that could work with that mechanic, but I don't think that this is one of them, on the grounds that it isn't actually a universally accepted premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-10-2015, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T22:41:38-07:00","id":658955,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you are right, but even so, who knows where Luna got the Rage, or what it means that she gave it to them. Will is obviously Weaverish, Englings recharge in the Flux, and the Wyrm has corrupted the Rage of the Garou. It seems that the Wyrn's talons are a over Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T23:18:48-07:00","id":659020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/658905-a-gift-proposal?p=658955#post658955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps you are right, but even so, who knows where Luna got the Rage, or what it means that she gave it to them. Will is obviously Weaverish,</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? It keeps you balanced. Balance is meeting in the middle at the Gaian point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Englings recharge in the Flux, </div> </div> </div>Things of all kinds do more than just &quot;recharge&quot; in Flux. They also tend to change and warp in various ways. It's a factor of new beginnings, rather than a statement that the Wyld is all Gnosis everywhere. Especially since Gnosis, as a Trait among Garou and Fera, is their connection to the spirit, which is definitely not just the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the Wyrm has corrupted the Rage of the Garou. It seems that the Wyrn's talons are a over Rage. </div> </div> </div>That interpretation goes against the metatextual maxim of making consequences of actions stand out as their own punishment or reward. The Garou aren't corrupted; they just keep making extremely short-sighted decisions with hot heads. There's actually not a cosmic evil to be blamed there, any more than the Wyrm is behind all human actions. It just takes advantage of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:30:32-07:00","id":659103,"title":"","content":"Also, The Abyss is not a Wyrm realm. What is it with people trying to shoehorn the Triat into everything? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T07:25:42-07:00","id":659357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/658905-a-gift-proposal?p=659103#post659103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, The Abyss is not a Wyrm realm. What is it with people trying to shoehorn the Triat into everything? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrall of the Wyrm was a bad example to set the stage for future examples of the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T00:11:39-07:00","id":662751,"title":"","content":"I thought the Abyss was supposed to represent the &quot;soul of the Wyrm&quot; according to Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Edit: and that the Sense Wyrm Gift showed everything in the Abyss to be Wyrm tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-13-2015, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T15:12:03-07:00","id":663509,"title":"","content":"Erm. No. No one knows that the Abyss really is and where it came from. They just know it scared the heebie jeebies out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:34:17-07:00","id":664645,"title":"","content":"Considering that the Abyss essentially represents the end of things, I don't see how it could <i>not</i> be associated with the Wyrm. Whether it's affiliated with the Wyrm of Corruption is another question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T13:13:04-07:00","id":664663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/658905-a-gift-proposal?p=664645#post664645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the Abyss essentially represents the end of things, I don't see how it could <i>not</i> be associated with the Wyrm. Whether it's affiliated with the Wyrm of Corruption is another question.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have the same kind of feel and yet be a freaky unknown. See also the mysterious Inquisitors that are after information on Pentex but appear to have no particular place in the ranks of Corruption even though they stink of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}